## What this predicate means

**A `realized-by` B** — B makes A concrete / actual (inverse of `realizes`).  The author-side advertisement: "this abstraction has known instantiations."

Common shapes:
- A plan realized-by the session-log of its execution
- A design realized-by the artifact that embodies it
- A pattern realized-by an implementation memorial

